---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { loadData } from '../lib/data.js';
const data = await loadData();
const genYear = new Date(data.generated_at).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<Base
  title="About & Methodology"
  description="How the Nepal Macro Overview is built: World Bank and IMF data stored in Neon Postgres, pre-rendered with Astro, refreshed weekly by GitHub Actions, deployable to Cloudflare Pages or Vercel."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Methodology</p>
    <h1>About this project</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      A complete, automatically refreshed macroeconomic and financial profile of Nepal — {data.indicators.length} indicators
      spanning growth and output, prices, the external sector, public finances, external debt, the financial system,
      and population and poverty. The entire site is pre-rendered HTML with zero client-side JavaScript, so it is fast
      at the edge and fully readable by search engines.
    </p>

    <h2>Data sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>World Bank, World Development Indicators</strong> — historical annual series, 2000 onward
        (GDP, remittances, FDI, trade, external debt, credit, broad money, population, poverty).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>IMF, World Economic Outlook</strong> — historical values plus staff projections through 2030
        (real growth, inflation, nominal GDP, GDP per capita, current account, government debt).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Pipeline</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>A Python script (<code>scripts/refresh_data.py</code>) pulls the latest series from the public World Bank API and the IMF DataMapper API.</li>
      <li>Results are upserted into a Neon serverless Postgres database and written to <code>data/snapshot.json</code>.</li>
      <li>Astro pre-renders every page at build time — reading from Neon when <code>DATABASE_URL</code> is set, otherwise from the snapshot.</li>
      <li>GitHub Actions runs this whole loop weekly (Mondays 06:00 UTC) and deploys the static output to the edge.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Last data refresh: <strong>{genYear}</strong>. Values marked “proj.” are IMF staff projections, not recorded outcomes.</p>

    <h2>Deployment</h2>
    <p>
      The build output is a plain static folder (<code>dist/</code>), ready for Cloudflare Pages, Cloudflare Workers Static Assets,
      Vercel, Netlify, or any static host. The included GitHub Action deploys to Cloudflare Pages when the
      <code>CLOUDFLARE_DEPLOY</code> repository variable is set to <code>true</code>. For Vercel, import the repository
      and add <code>DATABASE_URL</code> as an environment variable — no further configuration is needed.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      This site is for research and education. Figures are reproduced from public databases without modification;
      consult the original sources for official definitions and revisions. Nothing here is investment advice.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
